@@ -65,6 +65,19 @@ motion jump deterministically to their target while configured blinks remain act
 `renderAvatarDefinition` renders a static semantic expression. `renderAvatarFrame` renders an
 animated frame. Both return paths, visibility and resolved colors without creating DOM nodes.
 
+## Depth-aware body-node fragments
+
+Pass `{ occlusion: 'depth-aware' }` to `renderAvatar`, or as the trailing render-policy argument
+to `renderAvatarDefinition` and `renderAvatarFrame`, when a renderer needs a body node to paint on
+both sides of the primary surface. `geometry.nodeFragments` then contains one stable, input-ordered
+`{ nodeId, backPath, frontPath }` record per body node. Either path can be empty; crossing nodes can
+have both paths in the same frame.
+
+The mode is opt-in. Existing `backPaths`, `frontPaths`, `backNodeIds`, and `frontNodeIds` remain the
+complete-node compatibility output, so a depth-aware renderer paints `nodeFragments` instead of both
+representations. Fragments reuse the node surface samples and shared pose, compare sampled camera
+depth against the primary surface, and regenerate whenever the pose changes.
+
 ## Entry points
 
 - `@bible-strong/avatar-core`: contract, validation, semantic catalog, playback and scene APIs.
